 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "InMemoryDB() starts empty. Records are addressed by key and hold field-value pairs (all strings). setData(key, field, value) stores value in the field, replacing an existing value and creating the record when needed. getData(key, field) returns the stored value, or \"\" when the record or field is absent. deleteData(key, field) removes the field and returns true, or returns false when the record or field is absent. scanData(key) returns every field of the record as the string \"field(value)\", ordered by field name (code point order); an absent or empty record gives an empty list. scanDataByPrefix(key, prefix) returns the same strings restricted to fields that start with prefix (the empty prefix matches every field). Every method call is answered in call order on one instance; void methods return nothing.",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
    "revision": null,
    "path": "projects/algorithm_solver/catalogue/authored/hack2hire-chunk15-b-20261028-v1/contracts.json",
